*> Acceptance test, lane bugsleep (operator report of try19: "no getting into the bed or getting out"; docs/protocol/12 section 7.2 step 6, 05c Player Command 0 STOP_SLEEPING, 53 pose SLEEPING):
*> in play, the pose SLEEPING of the own entity (Set Entity Data entries 6 and 14) locks the player: the movement keys do not move it and the Sneak key (Left Shift) sends Player Command
*> STOP_SLEEPING (0x2A, the entity id, action 0, data 0); the standing pose of the own entity wakes the player and the movement keys work again.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. ACC-BUGSLEEP-CONTROLS.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 COPY CLCONST.
 COPY CCSHIM.
 COPY CONTENT.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 01 WS-SERVER              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-THRESHOLD           BINARY-LONG VALUE -1.
 01 WS-TEXT                PIC X(1024).
 01 WS-KEY                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-DOWN                BINARY-LONG VALUE CC-EV-KEY-DOWN.
 01 WS-UP                  BINARY-LONG VALUE CC-EV-KEY-UP.
 01 WS-TICKS               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ID                  BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
 01 WS-POSE                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-PRESENT             BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-X                   BINARY-LONG VALUE 3.
 01 WS-Y                   BINARY-LONG VALUE 5.
 01 WS-Z                   BINARY-LONG VALUE 4.
 01 WS-ZERO                BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-ZERO2               BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-ZERO3               BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-HITS                BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     CALL "TEST-PLAY" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-SERVER
     MOVE 1 TO PL-ENTITY-ID
     CALL "TEST-STEP" USING CLIENT-STATE
     CALL "TEST-SERVER-READ-HEX" USING WS-SERVER WS-TEXT WS-THRESHOLD
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
*>   Asleep: the keys do not move the player.
     MOVE 2 TO WS-POSE
     MOVE 1 TO WS-PRESENT
     CALL "BSC-DATA" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-POSE WS-PRESENT WS-X WS-Y WS-Z
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "bugsleep controls: pose 2 of the own entity puts the player to sleep" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE PL-SLEEP TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE CC-KEY-W TO WS-KEY
     CALL "TEST-KEY-TICK" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KEY WS-DOWN
     MOVE 9 TO WS-TICKS
     CALL "TEST-TICKS" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-TICKS
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "bugsleep controls: ten ticks of W do not move a sleeping player" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-POSITION" USING CLIENT-STATE TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "0.5000/10.0000/0.5000" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE CC-KEY-W TO WS-KEY
     CALL "TEST-KEY-TICK" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KEY WS-UP
     CALL "TEST-SERVER-READ-HEX" USING WS-SERVER WS-TEXT WS-THRESHOLD
*>   The Sneak key leaves the bed.
     MOVE CC-KEY-LEFT-SHIFT TO WS-KEY
     CALL "TEST-KEY-TICK" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KEY WS-DOWN
     CALL "TEST-SERVER-READ-HEX" USING WS-SERVER WS-TEXT WS-THRESHOLD
     MOVE 0 TO WS-HITS
     INSPECT WS-TEXT TALLYING WS-HITS FOR ALL "2a010000"
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "bugsleep controls: Left Shift in bed sends Player Command STOP_SLEEPING (2a 01 00 00)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-HITS TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE CC-KEY-LEFT-SHIFT TO WS-KEY
     CALL "TEST-KEY-TICK" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KEY WS-UP
*>   The server stands the player up: pose 0.
     MOVE 0 TO WS-POSE
     MOVE 0 TO WS-PRESENT
     CALL "BSC-DATA" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-POSE WS-PRESENT WS-ZERO WS-ZERO2 WS-ZERO3
     MOVE "bugsleep controls: pose 0 of the own entity wakes the player" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE PL-SLEEP TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "TEST-SERVER-READ-HEX" USING WS-SERVER WS-TEXT WS-THRESHOLD
     MOVE CC-KEY-W TO WS-KEY
     CALL "TEST-KEY-TICK" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-KEY WS-DOWN
     MOVE 9 TO WS-TICKS
     CALL "TEST-TICKS" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-TICKS
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "bugsleep controls: awake, ten ticks of W move the player again (z over 1)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "1" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE "0" TO TL-OBSERVED
     IF PL-Z > 1
         MOVE "1" TO TL-OBSERVED
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     STOP RUN.
 END PROGRAM ACC-BUGSLEEP-CONTROLS.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. BSC-DATA.
*> USING CLIENT-STATE, entity id, pose, present (0 or 1), x, y, z: Set Entity Data with entry 6 (POSE) and entry 14 (OPTIONAL_BLOCK_POS, the sleeping position).
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY PROTO.
 COPY PROTO REPLACING LEADING ==PB-== BY ==MD-==.
 01 WS-READY               BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-CAPACITY            BINARY-LONG VALUE 1024.
 01 WS-DATA                BINARY-LONG VALUE 101.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 01 L-ID                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-POSE                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-PRESENT              BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-X                    BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-Y                    BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-Z                    BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING CLIENT-STATE L-ID L-POSE L-PRESENT L-X L-Y L-Z.
     IF WS-READY = 0
         CALL "PB-INIT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-CAPACITY
         MOVE 1 TO WS-READY
     END-IF
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER L-ID
     INITIALIZE MD-METADATA-ENTRY
     MOVE 6 TO MD-MD-INDEX
     MOVE MD-MDS-POSE TO MD-MD-SERIALIZER
     MOVE L-POSE TO MD-MD-INT
     CALL "PB-PUT-ENTITY-METADATA" USING PB-BUFFER MD-METADATA-ENTRY
     INITIALIZE MD-METADATA-ENTRY-X
     MOVE 14 TO MD-MX-INDEX
     MOVE 11 TO MD-MX-SERIALIZER
     MOVE L-PRESENT TO MD-MX-PRESENT
     MOVE L-X TO MD-MX-POS-X
     MOVE L-Y TO MD-MX-POS-Y
     MOVE L-Z TO MD-MX-POS-Z
     CALL "PB-PUT-METADATA-ENTRY-X" USING PB-BUFFER MD-METADATA-ENTRY-X
     INITIALIZE MD-METADATA-ENTRY
     MOVE MD-MD-END TO MD-MD-INDEX
     CALL "PB-PUT-ENTITY-METADATA" USING PB-BUFFER MD-METADATA-ENTRY
     MOVE 0 TO PB-POS
     CALL "ENTITY-PACKET" USING CLIENT-STATE PB-BUFFER WS-DATA
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM BSC-DATA.

 COPY CLTEST.
